# Hospital Data Analysis Project

## Overview

This project is based on a dataset provided by King Fahd Hospital. The main objective was to clean, transform, and analyze the data, then build an interactive dashboard to support decision-making.

## Data Preparation

The project started with exploring the dataset and reviewing data types. Several inconsistencies were identified and corrected, especially incorrect data formats.

One of the key challenges was handling date and time fields. The original data contained combined date-time values, which were separated into two different columns (date and time). This resulted in having multiple date-related fields, creating a challenge when designing the data schema.

## Data Modeling Approach

To handle the date complexity, two approaches were considered:

* Keeping date fields separated as they are
* Using an alternating dimension technique in Power BI

Since the dataset was relatively small, the first approach was selected for simplicity and efficiency.

After that, primary and foreign keys were created to ensure proper relationships between tables, followed by building the data model.

## Dashboard Development

Once the data modeling was completed, interactive dashboards were created using Power BI. The dashboards provide clear insights into hospital operations and performance.

Two main dashboards were developed:

* Branch Performance Dashboard: to monitor and compare performance across different hospital branches
* Patient Analysis Dashboard: to analyze patient data, trends, and key metrics

## Insights and Recommendations

A final report was created to summarize key findings and provide actionable recommendations based on the analysis. These insights aim to support better decision-making and improve overall hospital performance.

## Tools and Technologies

* Power BI
* Data Cleaning and Transformation Techniques
* Data Modeling

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates the full data analysis workflow, starting from raw data cleaning to delivering interactive dashboards and business insights.
